{
  "_what": "Every five minutes reads due_tells() from the person's own history: each person (a thing whose scheme is told_about) with standing new statements whose meanings' tell_after has passed since the newest, batched, with the tell_words for that set of meanings (a cancel and a new booking together are 'moved the call'). For each it first claims the tell (tells, primary key thing and through), so the same changes are never told twice even when two runs overlap, then puts one ready action to the owner: when the person's next call starts within soon_minutes, a notice to call them now; else an email to the address the person used last, drafted by tool:ask-a-model from the history, scored by the owner's voice scorer (tool:score-writing-with-a-voice-adapter, mode draft), saved as a mail draft, and a notice about that draft. Any failed step after the claim gives the claim back, so the next look tells it; when the notice itself failed, the draft it would have named is removed after the claim is given back, so a retold person never leaves a second draft. The next call is the earliest starts_at of the person's bookings whose latest statement has no cancelled_at: the names a source's waiter row carries its values under (service-lists shape.carry).",
  "records": [
    {
      "payload": {
        "kind": "workflow-recipe",
        "id": "workflow:tell-the-owner-what-changed-for-each-person",
        "label": "Tell me what changed for each person, with one ready message",
        "job": "Every five minutes, read from the person's own history which people have new changes that have settled (due_tells: each meaning's tell_after, batched per person, told once), and for each put one ready action to the owner: a call to make now when their next call starts within soon_minutes, else one email drafted in the owner's voice, checked by the voice scorer and saved as a draft, which goes only after the owner says yes",
        "produces": "one notice to the owner for each person with settled new changes (never two for the same changes), each with one ready action: a call to make now, or a saved mail draft to send on their yes",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "history": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "Where the person's history is: credential_name, the vault name of its database connection"
            },
            "address_scheme": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The history scheme whose identifiers are where an email goes (its schemes row)"
            },
            "soon_minutes": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "A next call starting within this many minutes is a call to make now, not an email"
            },
            "voice": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "The owner's voice scorer settings for tool:score-writing-with-a-voice-adapter draft mode: adapter, base_model, criterion, min_paragraph_chars, decider_common_dir"
            },
            "mail": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "The owner's mail account the draft is saved in: provider and connection {connection_id}"
            }
          }
        },
        "wakes": [
          {
            "id": "every-five-minutes",
            "on": {
              "fact": {
                "kind": "due-time",
                "from": [
                  "run"
                ],
